    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "IMMACULATELY PRESENTED 4-BEDROOM BUNGALOW, ON A SPACIOUS SITE, IN AN EXCELLECT LOCATION, JUST 4km TO LONGFORD TOWN AND THE N4.\r\n\r\nIt gives us great pleasure here at Davis Auctioneers, to bring to the market this superb four-bedroom bungalow, just a few minutes’ drive from the N4 and Longford Town. This very well cared for home, maintained brilliantly both internally and externally, comes to the market at a time when bungalows are in very short supply.\r\n\r\nLocated at one of the most sought-after residential addresses, this fine bungalow property, is just a five-minute drive from Longford town centre. Positioned along the R198 at Cahannagh, the main Drumlish Road, we expect huge interest in ‘Beacon Hill’, a unique family home.\r\n\r\nCahanngh is within easy reach of Longford Town centre, which boast the Mall Complex, an 18-hole golf course, swimming pool, sports complex, G.A.A. Soccer and Rugby clubs, among many other amenities and services. \r\n\r\nThere is a large retail park (N4 Axis centre) with restaurant, shops, 24-hour gym and coffee shop within a five-minute drive, while Longford train station which is on the Sligo-Dublin line, is just a ten-minute drive away.\r\n\r\nThis spacious residence is cosy in its lay out, with double doors leading to a rear patio area, and large site with great potential for further development. Brilliantly situated with Drumlish, Killoe, Newtownforbes and Longford Town just a few minutes drive away. The much-desired national schools of Melview, as well as Enybegs are just a short drive.\r\n\r\nThe well laid out accommodation comprises of a wide entrance hall, sitting-room, kitchen-dining room, four bedrooms (master ensuite), a family bathroom as well as a utility area off the kitchen with door access to the rear. \r\n\r\nOne of the many outstanding features of this fine property, is the attic roof space, that has been specifically designed to facilitate easy future conversion, complemented by a spacious hallway providing excellent potential for additional living accommodation. The enclosed dog area to the rear of the site, as well as the sandstone entrance walls and tarmacadam driveway are some of the many outstanding features of this gem.\r\n\r\nViewing of this property is highly recommended by the sole auctioneers. \r\n\r\nPlease contact us on 043 3350555 or call to us at 53 Main Street,  Longford to arrange your viewing.\r\n\r\nEircode: N39 F9T1\r\nFolio No: LD13658FF (C.0.25 hectares)"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance hall: 3.05m x 4.55m\r\nSitting room: 4.85m x 3.60m\r\nKitchen/dining room: 4.20m x 6.80m\r\nUtility: 1.10m x 2.30m\r\nBed 1: 3.50m x 3.35m\r\nEn-suite: 1.40m x 2.10m\r\nBed 2: 3.30m x 2.65m\r\nBed 3: 3.40m x 3.65m"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Extensive site with potential for further development\r\n\r\nWide entrance hall and attic roof space designed for easy conversion\r\n\r\nMinutes to Melview and Enybegs National Schools\r\n\r\nNewtownfobes, Drumlish, Ballinalee, Killoe & Longford Town just a few minutes drive\r\n\r\nSecure Boundary walls, fencing and hedging\r\n\r\nOn the Cavan-Longford daily bus route\r\n\r\nSouth & East facing rear garden\r\n\r\nSandstone Entrance walls and piers\r\n\r\nFitted Wardrobes\r\n\r\nVehicle access to the side and rear of the dwelling\r\n\r\nTarmacadam Driveway\r\n\r\nFitted Utility with back door access\r\n\r\nOil fired central heating\r\n\r\nFireplace in the Sitting Room\r\n\r\nDouble Glazed Pvc Windows and Doors\r\n\r\nMain Water & Treatment system\r\n\r\nJust 3km to the N4 national route\r\n\r\nHighly desirable location\r\n\r\n10-minute drive to the train station\r\n\r\nIdeal owner occupier residence \r\n\r\nFibre broadband available\r\n\r\nCreche facilities close buy \r\n\r\nNumerous national and post primary schools available\r\n\r\nBus service to Secondary Schools in Longford and Moyne CS\r\n\r\nLongford Train Station: 10 Minute drive\r\n\r\n7 Trains a day on the Dublin-Sligo Line\r\n\r\nCommute to Dublin- 1 hour & 20 mins"
